decimal coverage: {"decimalFileOpensIn": 1910, "glossableYears": [{"endYear": 1949, "scheduleId": "1910-1949", "startYear": 1910}, {"endYear": 1959, "scheduleId": "1950-1959", "startYear": 1950}, {"endYear": 1963, "scheduleId": "1960-1963", "startYear": 1960}], "keyOutsideGlossableYears": "no-gloss", "notShipped": [], "note": "A key is glossable only when the document's own date falls inside one of `glossableYears`. Outside them this file has NO gloss \u2014 do not compose one from a schedule that does not govern the key's era. The classification was renumbered in 1950, so composing across that year returns a plausible WRONG reading rather than a miss: `411` reads as Claims under the 1910\u20131949 schedule where the editors gloss `411.48` as Poland, and `48` reads as British Africa \u2014 and `48` is live in TWO of this schedule's vocabularies at once (country `British Africa`, class-8 subject `Calamitie
